Usage: ruralz bundle diff FROM TO [FLAGS]

Compare FROM with TO.

FROM and TO are each a Bundle directory, a rendered Bundle file, a saved
ruralz node dump file, an admin URL such as https://node-a.example:9901 whose
/config/dump is read, or - for standard input (one side at most). Both sides run
through the configuration pipeline and compare as validated states. --from-env
and --to-env stand in for --env on one side. Exits 0 without changes, 1 with
changes and 2 for errors. Revision sources (rev-<12 hex>, sha256:<64 hex>,
oci://) are Planned (M2).

Arguments:
  FROM  Bundle directory or file, saved dump, admin URL, or -
  TO    Same forms as FROM

Flags:
  --admin-token-file PATH       Operator admin token file (default $RURALZ_ADMIN_TOKEN_FILE)
  --ca-file PATH                Extra trust anchors (PEM), added to the system roots
  --client-cert PATH            Client certificate (PEM) for admin mTLS over https
  --client-key PATH             Unencrypted PEM key of --client-cert
  --env NAME                    Render with this Environment's overlay and variables, read from --environments
  --environments FILE           Local Environment resources
  --from-admin-token-file PATH  Operator admin token file for FROM (default --admin-token-file)
  --from-client-cert PATH       Client certificate for FROM (default --client-cert)
  --from-client-key PATH        Key of --from-client-cert (default --client-key)
  --from-env NAME               Environment of FROM, in place of --env
  --help                        Print this help
  --output text|json            Output format (text or json, default text)
  --timeout DURATION            Deadline of each admin call that does not stream (default 5m; 0 means none)
  --to-admin-token-file PATH    Operator admin token file for TO (default --admin-token-file)
  --to-client-cert PATH         Client certificate for TO (default --client-cert)
  --to-client-key PATH          Key of --to-client-cert (default --client-key)
  --to-env NAME                 Environment of TO, in place of --env
